Name the baseline attributes in the layout trace.

CiderAttributeName had no case for NSLayoutAttributeFirstBaseline or NSLayoutAttributeLastBaseline
and fell through to "other". Both are handled by CiderRecordAttribute and by CiderAttributeValue,
so the solver supports them; only the NAME was missing.

A name that lies costs an investigation. The trace read

  all: NSTextField 0x... .other == NSButton 0x... .other * 1 + 0

for the rule that vertically aligns every label in iA Writer Preferences with its control, and an
attribute the solver supports looked like one it had dropped. The nib says the value is 12, which
is firstBaseline, used 8 times in GeneralPreferences.nib. With the name in place the same line
reads

  all: NSTextField .firstBaseline == NSButton .firstBaseline * 1 + 0

and the pass 2 line below it shows the rule being applied and resolving, which is what said the
labels were innocent.

WHAT THAT THEN FOUND, recorded here because the trace is what found it. Both labels correctly
follow their own button by baseline, and both resolve to y=417, because the two buttons really are
at the same y. The tree says why:

  NSStackView(0x...250cb0) 182x38 at 207,395      the outer stack, a direct child of the pane
    NSStackView(0x...5ce40) 182x38 at 0,0         child A
    NSStackView(0x...53270) 161x38 at 0,0         child B

Two arranged subviews at the same local origin, exactly on top of each other. -[NSStackView
initWithCoder:] creates an EMPTY _arrangedSubviews and decodes only orientation and spacing, so
every nib loaded stack view has nothing to arrange and -layout walks an empty list. The constraint
solver deliberately skips arranged subviews because the stack is supposed to own them, so nothing
places these at all. The archive carries NSStackViewHasFlatViewHierarchy true, which says the
arranged views ARE the decoded subviews, and that is the next fix.

Gates: dts 69 of 69, patch record PASS, roster sweep 7 of 7 CONTENT and roster input 7 of 7, byte
identical, with Money Manager Ex looked at.

--- a/AppKit/NSView.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSView.m
@@ -5146,7 +5146,13 @@
     case NSLayoutAttributeHeight:   return "height";
     case NSLayoutAttributeCenterX:  return "centerX";
     case NSLayoutAttributeCenterY:  return "centerY";
+    case NSLayoutAttributeFirstBaseline: return "firstBaseline";
+    case NSLayoutAttributeLastBaseline:  return "lastBaseline";
     case NSLayoutAttributeNotAnAttribute: return "none";
+    /* A NAME THAT LIES COSTS AN INVESTIGATION. Both baselines are handled by the recorder and by
+     * CiderAttributeValue, and only this switch was missing them, so the trace read
+     * "NSTextField .other == NSButton .other" and an attribute the solver supports looked like one
+     * it had dropped. iA Writer label rows were chased on that reading. */
     default: return "other";
     }
 }
